  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1016 PM CDT FRI OCT 23 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery this evening reveals an upper ridge pushing\nacross the Plains as an upper low over Nevada cuts into it  At\nthe surface, high pressure remains in control of the region. Dry\nconditions look to continue over the next week as the upper ridge\nexpands and moisture remains limited. Temperatures will also\nremain relatively stable under the ridge, with highs ranging in\nthe mid to upper 70s, and lows in the 40s. The exception to this\nwill be Monday night, when the apex of the ridge will slightly\nshift east. This will allow for cooler air to push farther south\nunder the CAD wedge. There is a low (~10%) chance for a few\nlocations across our eastern areas to dip into the upper\n30s. Otherwise, light winds and clear skies will promote patchy\nriver fog overnight into the early morning hours daily over the\nnext few days.\n\nThe upper ridge will begin to break down late in the week as a\ntrough approaches from the west. This will likely lead to a brief\nperiod of warmer temps ahead of our next cold front.\n\n95/Castillo",
